It will soon take OC Transpo riders up to three minutes longer to travel between the west end and downtown Ottawa once another section of the Transitway closes Sunday, forcing hundreds of buses onto Scott and Albert streets.
All eastbound buses will be diverted off the Transitway at Merton Street to new bus-only lanes on Scott and Albert streets. Westbound buses will now enter the Transitway at Merton, where a new set of traffic signals has been installed.
This marks the first time a portion of the dedicated busway has closed west of downtown as part of the conversion to light rail. The stretch between Blair and Hurdman stations closed last June, and the stretch between Hurdman and Lees shut down before Christmas.
Unlike the changes in the east end — which saw some routes leapfrog Transitway stations they formerly stopped at and one station closed completely — the closure of the Transitway between Empress and Merton does not affect any of the routes that serve this area.
