(James Deuter). No doubt when author Charles Laurence wrote the play, which ran in London in 1972 and on Broadway in 1974, outrageous gay wit was still unusual enough to carry a whole show.
It isn`t these days, and while Laurence`s bitchy lines are stinging, frequently funny and, for the most part, wickedly unprintable, ''My Fat Friend'' doesn`t offer much sustenance beyond them.
